{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>How did you break through, etc.</b> The meaning is: since the hand of the first one would indicate that he was the one about to emerge before his brother, and even so this one pushed the first aside and obscured the fact that he had positioned himself before him — this proclaims a great degree [of strength]. And this is what it says <b>מַה פָּרַצְתָּ</b> ('How did you break through'), in the manner of the verse (Psalms 104:24): ״מַה רַבּוּ מַעֲשֶׂיךָ״ and so forth. And her saying <b>עָלֶיךָ פָּרֶץ</b> ('upon you, a breach') explains her words — what the breach that he made was — and she said ״עָלֶיךָ פָּרֶץ״, meaning: for the one who extends his hand proclaims that he comes upon him in the insemination, for the one who enters last in the seed emerges first, and if so he came upon him and breached his fence and emerged first. And this is what it says ״עָלֶיךָ פָּרֶץ״ — understand it. And according to this, Peretz is first in the insemination and first in the birth, for upon him the kingship was poured to be established forever."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:58.708312477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}